### Goal Model Decomposition

The mission involves multi-robot systems collecting and delivering resources while handling battery constraints. The goal model is structured to reflect the sequential phases of collection and delivery, with parallel execution for efficiency and fallback mechanisms for battery management.

#### Goal Nodes

| Goal ID | Goal Text | Goal Type | Relation | Target Condition | Enquired Information | Runtime Annotation | Justification |
|---------|-----------|-----------|----------|------------------|-----------------------|--------------------|----------------|
| G1      | Deliver Required Resources to Requesting Agent | Achieve | - | All resources delivered to the correct location | - | - | Primary objective to achieve successful delivery. |
| G2      | Collection Phase | Perform | AND (G1) | Resources collected | - | # | Multiple robots can collect from different storages in parallel. |
| G3      | Delivery Phase | Perform | AND (G1) | Resources delivered | - | # | Multiple robots can deliver in parallel. |
| G2.1    | Retrieve Resources from Storage 1 | Perform | AND (G2) | Resources retrieved | - | ; | Sequential steps: send message, wait, retrieve. |
| G2.2    | Retrieve Resources from Storage 2 | Perform | AND (G2) | Resources retrieved | - | ; | Sequential steps: send message, wait, retrieve. |
| G3.1    | Deliver Resources to Destination 1 | Perform | AND (G3) | Resources delivered | - | ; | Sequential delivery steps. |
| G3.2    | Deliver Resources to Destination 2 | Perform | AND (G3) | Resources delivered | - | ; | Sequential delivery steps. |

#### Task Nodes

| Task ID | Task Title | Task Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|-----------|----------|----------|-------------------|----------------|
| AT2.1.1 | Send Message to Storage 1 | Send resource request | AND (G2.1) | Storage 1 | 1 | Single robot action. |
| AT2.1.2 | Wait for Retrieval | Wait for resources | AND (G2.1) | Storage 1 | 1 | Single robot action. |
| AT2.1.3 | Proceed to Next Storage | Move after retrieval | AND (G2.1) | Storage 1 | 1 | Single robot action. |
| AT3.1.1 | Deliver Batch 1 | Deliver part of resources | AND (G3.1) | Destination | 1 | Single robot action. |
| AT3.1.2 | Return to Charging | Handle low battery | Fallback (G3.1) | Charging Station | 1 | Fallback for battery issues. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**: Both collection and delivery are required for mission success.
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [OR]**: Multiple storages can be handled in parallel.
- **G2.1 -> AT2.1.1, AT2.1.2, AT2.1.3 [AND]**: Sequential steps for resource retrieval.
- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [OR]**: Multiple delivery points can be handled in parallel.
- **G3.1 -> AT3.1.1, AT3.1.2 [FALLBACK]**: Fallback for low battery during delivery.

### Summary

The goal model is designed to handle resource collection and delivery efficiently using multiple robots in parallel. Each phase is broken down into tasks that ensure sequential execution for accuracy, with fallback mechanisms for battery management to ensure mission success.
